  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Helping local communities in West Aceh to reduce their vulnerability to disaster</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD supported YPK in past years to establish micro-credit institutions, known as LEMs, in nine villages in West Aceh.   These LEMs made small loans available to local people who were badly affected by the December 2004 Tsunami or by the widespread violence and conflict which prevailed in Aceh in the years leading up to the tsunami disaster.  The loans were to enable them to resume their former livelihoods or else start new businesses.  Since 2010, YPK has been working with the same villages to establish community-based organisations which are then supported to draw up Action Plans for disaster preparedness and adaptation to climate change.  YPK also holds workshops and disaster mapping exercises at district-level, to help the local government link up with the efforts of the grassroots communities and so foster the mainstreaming of disaster risk reduction.  In implementing this project, YPK will meet regularly with SKS, which is doing similar work in North Aceh, to share experiences and learning and start to develop provincial level advocacy initiatives.</narrative>
  </description>
